<title>UK: HORSE RACING-FRANKIE DETTORI FACTFILE.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-FRANKIE DETTORI FACTFILE.</headline>
<dateline>ASCOT, England 1996-09-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is factfile on</p>
<p>Frankie Dettori who won on all his seven mounts on Saturday:</p>
<p>Born: December 15, 1970. Father Gianfranco champion jockey</p>
<p>in Italy who won English 2,000 Guineas on Bolkonski and Wollow.</p>
<p>Apprenticeship: With Luca Cumani.</p>
<p>First winner: Billy Pitt at Turin in November 1986.</p>
<p>First winner in Britain: Lizzy Hare at Goodwood in June 1987.</p>
<p>Champion apprentice: 1989 (75 winners).</p>
<p>Champion jockey: 1994.</p>
<p>First century of winners in a season: 1990 (first teenager</p>
<p>to ride 100 winners in a season since Lester Piggott).</p>
<p>Best total: 233 winners in 1994.</p>
<p>Leading successes:</p>
<p>Breeders' Cup Mile:  Barathea in 1994.</p>
<p>British classic winners: </p>
<p>Balanchine - Oaks 1994, Moonshell - Oaks 1995, Classic</p>
<p>Cliche - St Leger 1995, Mark of Esteem - 2,000 Guineas 1996,</p>
<p>Shantou - St Leger 1996.</p>
<p>French Derby winner: Polytain 1992.</p>
<p>Irish Derby winner: Balanchine 1994.</p>
<p>King George VI And Queen Elizabeth Diamond Stakes winner:</p>
<p>Lammtarra 1995.</p>
<p>Prix de l'Arc de Triomphe winner: Lammtarra 1995.</p>
<p>Other big winners: Drum Taps (Ascot Gold Cup 1992 and </p>
<p>1993), Halling (Juddmonte International at York 1996).</p>
<p>Went through the seven-race card at Ascot, September 1996.</p>
</text>
